     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults:\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day.\n\nAt this dose the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was confirmed. I'd recommend checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
